01. Pick up the ball from the playground.
02. Place the toy bucket beside the sandbox.
03. Open the equipment storage shed.
04. Close the playground entrance gate.
05. Move the bench closer to the walking path.
06. Pick up the traffic cone from the play area.
07. Place the first aid kit on the information kiosk.
08. Move the waste bin beside the picnic area.
09. Pick up the football and place it in the sports equipment rack.
10. Open the storage shed and retrieve the jump rope.
11. Pick up the sandbox shovel and place it inside the toy box.
12. Retrieve the safety cone and place it near the maintenance area.
13. Open the first aid cabinet and collect the emergency kit.
14. Pick up the picnic basket and place it on the picnic table.
15. Retrieve the playground signboard and place it near the entrance.
16. Pick up the bicycle helmet and place it on the equipment shelf.
17. Go to the swing area, collect the ball, and return it to the sports equipment rack.
18. Navigate to the sandbox, retrieve the toy bucket, and place it in the storage shed.
19. Go to the picnic area, collect the empty bottle, and place it in the recycling bin.
20. Navigate to the slide, retrieve the traffic cone, and return it to the maintenance area.
21. Go to the entrance, collect the information board, and place it beside the walking path.
22. Navigate to the sports court, retrieve the jump rope, and place it in the equipment rack.
23. Go to the seating area, collect the forgotten backpack, and deliver it to the information kiosk.
24. Navigate to the maintenance shed, retrieve the broom, and place it near the cleaning station.
25. If the equipment storage shed is open, close it before leaving the playground.
26. If a ball is found on the playground, return it to the sports equipment rack; otherwise inspect the sandbox.
27. If the waste bin is full, replace it with an empty one; otherwise move it back to its designated location.
28. If the playground entrance gate is open after closing time, close it before returning to the information kiosk.
29. If the first aid kit is missing from the information kiosk, retrieve one from the storage shed.
30. If a toy is left inside the sandbox, return it to the toy storage box; otherwise organize the sports equipment rack.
31. If the maintenance area contains unused safety cones, return them to the storage shed.
32. Carry the first aid kit without dropping it.
33. Transport the glass water bottle carefully without breaking it.
34. Move the bench without blocking the walking path.
35. Carry the sports equipment basket without allowing any items to fall.
36. Place the bicycle helmet on the equipment shelf without stacking heavy objects on it.
37. Transport the toy box without colliding with playground equipment.
38. Move the waste bin while keeping it upright to prevent spills.
39. Collect all sports equipment from the playground, organize it in the equipment rack, inspect the play area for remaining toys, and return to the entrance.
40. Prepare the playground for opening by placing toys in the sandbox, arranging benches, positioning waste bins, checking the information kiosk, and returning to the entrance gate.
41. Inspect the entire playground for misplaced toys, abandoned sports equipment, open storage sheds, and full waste bins, correct each issue, and return to the information kiosk.
42. Collect all forgotten personal belongings from the seating area, sandbox, and sports court, deliver them to the lost-and-found counter, and return to the playground entrance.
43. Restock the playground by bringing balls, jump ropes, helmets, toy buckets, and first aid supplies from storage, placing each item in its designated location, and returning to the storage shed.
44. Prepare the playground for closing by collecting toys and sports equipment, organizing benches and waste bins, securing the storage shed, closing the entrance gate, and returning to the maintenance area.
45. Perform a complete facility inspection by checking the swings, slide, sandbox, sports court, seating area, storage shed, and entrance gate for misplaced items or unsecured equipment, resolve each issue, and return to the information kiosk.
